data-math=\"P-50\\cos35^\\circ=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow P=50\\cos35^\\circ=41.0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q-50\\sin35^\\circ=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow Q=50\\sin35^\\circ=28.7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q5","number":5,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> An object of mass 2 kg is held in equilibrium, suspended by two light, inextensible strings as shown in each of the diagrams. The tensions in the string are given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N.</p><p>In each case, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q5a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q5b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q5c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\\cos45^\\circ-T_1\\cos35^\\circ=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\\sin45^\\circ+T_1\\sin35^\\circ-2\\times9.8=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow T_1=14.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=16.3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\\sin42^\\circ-T_1\\sin18^\\circ=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\\cos42^\\circ+T_1\\cos18^\\circ-2\\times9.8=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow T_1=15.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=6.99\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\\cos50^\\circ-T_1\\cos50^\\circ=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2\\sin50^\\circ+T_1\\sin50^\\circ-2\\times9.8=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow T_1=12.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=12.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>A particle of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg is held in equilibrium, suspended by two light, inextensible strings as shown in each of the diagrams. One of the strings has tension <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>In each case, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q6a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q6b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-14\\sin70^\\circ=0\\Rightarrow T=13.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"14\\cos70^\\circ-9.8m=0\\Rightarrow m=0.487\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5-T\\cos60^\\circ=0\\Rightarrow T=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\sin60^\\circ-9.8m=0\\Rightarrow m=0.884\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A particle of weight 10 N is held in equilibrium, suspended by two light, inextensible strings as shown in the following diagram. The tension in the horizontal string is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N. The second string is pulling with a tension of 15 N at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the horizontal in the opposite direction to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q7.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15\\sin\\theta^\\circ-10=0\\Rightarrow\\theta=41.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-15\\cos\\theta^\\circ=0\\Rightarrow T=11.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>A particle of weight 4 N is held in equilibrium, suspended by two light, inextensible strings as shown in the following diagram. The tension in the horizontal string is 18 N. The second string is pulling with a tension of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the horizontal in the opposite direction to the first string.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q8.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"18-T\\cos\\theta^\\circ=0\\Rightarrow T\\cos\\theta^\\circ=18\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\\sin\\theta^\\circ-4=0\\Rightarrow T\\sin\\theta^\\circ=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=12.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=18.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q9","number":9,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=10\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> A box of mass 4 kg is suspended by a cable, which makes an angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with a vertical wall. A horizontal rope keeps the box in equilibrium.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q9.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Calculate the tension in the cable giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Calculate the tension in the rope giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the angle at which the tension in the cable and the rope is the same.</p></li><li><p>Find the range of angles at which the tension in the rope is less than the weight of the box.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1\\cos\\theta^\\circ-40=0\\Rightarrow T_1=\\frac{40}{\\cos\\theta^\\circ}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2-\\frac{40}{\\cos\\theta^\\circ}\\times\\sin\\theta^\\circ=0\\Rightarrow T_2=40\\tan\\theta^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{40}{\\cos\\theta^\\circ}=40\\frac{\\sin\\theta^\\circ}{\\cos\\theta^\\circ}\\Rightarrow\\sin\\theta=1\\Rightarrow90^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40\\tan\\theta^\\circ&lt;40\\Rightarrow\\tan\\theta^\\circ&lt;1\\Rightarrow\\theta&lt;45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore0^\\circ\\le\\theta&lt;45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q10","number":10,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use exact values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> A particle of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg is held in equilibrium by two strings, each inclined at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the horizontal. The tension in each string is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q10.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T=\\frac{mg}{2\\sin\\theta^\\circ}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when the particle has weight 5 N and</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"60^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> approaches <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\\sin\\theta^\\circ+T\\sin\\theta^\\circ-mg=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow2T\\sin\\theta^\\circ=mg\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow T=\\frac{mg}{2\\sin\\theta^\\circ}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=\\frac5{2\\sin45^\\circ}=\\frac52\\sqrt2=3.54\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (3SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=\\frac5{2\\sin60^\\circ}=\\frac53\\sqrt3=2.89\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (3SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\to90^\\circ,T\\to2.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Two ropes are hung from a ceiling, 2 metres apart and are connected at their other ends. The length of rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are 1.4 metres and 1.6 metres respectively.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>A crate of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg is attached at the end of both rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The system is in equilibrium. Show that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acute angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the ceiling is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos\\alpha=\\frac{17}{28}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>the acute angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the ceiling is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos\\beta=\\frac{23}{32}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol><p>The tensions in rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and rope <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{T_B}{T_A}=\\frac{136}{161}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_A=322\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li><p>find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.6^2=1.4^2+2^2-2\\times1.4\\times2\\times\\cos\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\cos\\alpha=\\frac{1.6^2-1.4^2-2^2}{-2\\times1.4\\times2}=\\frac{17}{28}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.4^2=1.6^2+2^2-2\\times1.6\\times2\\times\\cos\\beta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\cos\\beta=\\frac{1.4^2-1.6^2-2^2}{-2\\times1.6\\times2}=\\frac{23}{32}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_B\\cos\\beta-T_A\\cos\\alpha=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{23}{32}T_B-\\frac{17}{28}T_A=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{23}{32}T_B=\\frac{17}{28}T_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{T_B}{T_A}=\\frac{\\frac{17}{28}}{\\frac{23}{32}}=\\frac{136}{161}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_B=272\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"322\\sin\\alpha+272\\sin\\beta-mg=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{28^2-17^2}=3\\sqrt{55}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\alpha=\\frac{3\\sqrt{55}}{28}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{32^2-23^2}=3\\sqrt{55}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\beta=\\frac{3\\sqrt{55}}{32}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"322\\times\\frac{3\\sqrt{55}}{28}+272\\times\\frac{3\\sqrt{55}}{32}-mg=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"60\\sqrt{55}-mg=0\\Rightarrow m=\\frac{60\\sqrt{55}}g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q12","number":12,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use Triangles of Forces and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> An object of weight 50 N is suspended, in equilibrium, by two light inextensible strings <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which make angles of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the horizontal as shown in the diagram below:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q12.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The tension in string <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N and the tension in string <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the triangle of forces for these forces.</p></li><li><p>Hence determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/solutions/assets/diagrams/s12a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{50}{\\sin75^\\circ}=\\frac{T_B}{\\sin60^\\circ}\\Rightarrow T_B=44.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{50}{\\sin75^\\circ}=\\frac{T_A}{\\sin45^\\circ}\\Rightarrow T_A=36.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows a system of forces in equilibrium:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q13.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the triangle of forces for these forces.</p></li><li><p>Find the range of possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the system to remain in equilibrium.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/solutions/assets/diagrams/s13a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"180^\\circ-45^\\circ=135^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\theta&lt;135\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>A particle of mass 2 kg is suspended by two light inextensible strings <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which make an angles of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"35^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the vertical respectively, as shown in the diagram below:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q14.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The tension in string <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N and the tension in string <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the triangle of forces for the forces acting on the object.</p></li><li><p>Hence determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/solutions/assets/diagrams/s14a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{19.6}{\\sin115^\\circ}=\\frac{T_B}{\\sin35^\\circ}\\Rightarrow T_B=12.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{19.6}{\\sin115^\\circ}=\\frac{T_A}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\Rightarrow T_A=10.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>An object of weight <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N is attached to one end of a light inextensible string of length 8 cm. The other end is attached to a vertical wall at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. A horizontal force of magnitude 10 N is applied to the object. The particle is in equilibrium with the string taut, where it lies 5 cm from the wall.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q15.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a triangle of forces for the forces acting on the object.</p></li></ol><p>Hence find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>the tension in the string.</p></li><li><p>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the mass of the object.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac58\\right)=51.3^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/solutions/assets/diagrams/s15a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=\\frac{10}{\\frac58}=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w=\\sqrt{16^2-10^2}=2\\sqrt{39}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w=12.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Mass is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2\\sqrt{39}}{9.8}=1.27\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg</p>","<p>1.3 kg (2 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.52-q16","number":16,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use exact values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong></p><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q16: Compound Angle Formulae</strong> A small box B of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg is held in equilibrium by two light strings, one attached to a vertical wall which has a tension of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_W\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N and one to the horizontal floor which has a tension of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_F\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N. They make an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the wall and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the floor respectively.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/questions/assets/diagrams/q16.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a triangle of forces for the forces acting on the box.</p></li></ol><p>Hence or otherwise, given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, show that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_W=\\sqrt3mg\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_F=mg\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>Angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is increased and the angle of the string with the floor becomes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The system remains in equilibrium.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li><p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T_W=\\frac{mg}{\\cos\\alpha^\\circ-\\sin\\alpha^\\circ}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.52/solutions/assets/diagrams/s16a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{T_W}{\\sin120^\\circ}=\\frac{mg}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\Rightarrow T_W=\\frac{mg\\sin120^\\circ}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\sqrt3mg\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{T_F}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\frac{mg}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\Rightarrow T_F=mg\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{T_W}{\\sin135^\\circ}=\\frac{mg}{\\sin(45-\\alpha)^\\circ}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin(45-\\alpha)^\\circ=\\sin45^\\circ\\cos\\alpha^\\circ-\\cos45^\\circ\\sin\\alpha^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=\\frac{\\sqrt2}2(\\cos\\alpha^\\circ-\\sin\\alpha^\\circ)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\frac{T_W}{\\frac{\\sqrt2}2}=\\frac{mg}{\\frac{\\sqrt2}2(\\cos\\alpha^\\circ-\\sin\\alpha^\\circ)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>which gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_W=\\frac{mg}{\\cos\\alpha^\\circ-\\sin\\alpha^\\circ}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]}]